  "body": "The selected [PR #589](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/589) R439 word keeps helper470 for one late read after source77\nhas entered frame186. At that actual caller boundary, source77 is unchanged\nand receiver444 can enter frame186 before its next gate. This construction\nreads source77 directly, deletes helper470, rebuilds literal C and dirty-target\nD, and recounts the complete nine-stage hosted schedule on the same upstream\nword.\n\nReview files: [Proof and scope](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/e309e17f83f5759b1ea1fa24a76f24838784cb4d/research/bit-boundary-persistence/PROOF.md) \u00b7 [Evidence](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/e309e17f83f5759b1ea1fa24a76f24838784cb4d/research/bit-boundary-persistence/CERTIFICATE.json) \u00b7 [Source pins and credit](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/e309e17f83f5759b1ea1fa24a76f24838784cb4d/research/bit-boundary-persistence/SOURCES.json).\n\nThe result is R438, **24,305 \u2192 24,248 local ADDs** and\n**904,896 \u2192 904,320 paid recursive children**. The full exact bit invoice\nimproves **c = 0.001733427039589844234749 \u2192 0.001734176288479865766692**.\nAll returned idle rank, source access, restoration, copied totals and helper\noccupancy are paid. Live stock and precision allowances are unchanged.\n**No new kappa:** the selected complex supplier still binds.\n\nValidation includes every dirty local column, original H1-H5, independent\nliteral records, original C++ legality and 5/9/11-stage checks on both words,\n96 omitted-bridge controls, both complete parent and residual-hosting audits,\nand two exact moment engines. Six new controls reject source-lifetime,\nframe, restoration, compensation and omitted-idle-charge defects. Full paths,\nsource pins, exact certificate, proof and reproduction command are in\n[research/bit-boundary-persistence/](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/tree/e309e17f83f5759b1ea1fa24a76f24838784cb4d/research/bit-boundary-persistence).\n\n```sh\nBOOST_INCLUDE=/opt/homebrew/include python3 -I -B research/bit-boundary-persistence/verify.py --output /tmp/r438-source-boundary\n```\n\nBase [8bddbee377e2f3ce1f1247196c4b290d55767d20](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/8bddbee377e2f3ce1f1247196c4b290d55767d20). Only this research package\nis added. [PR #980](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/980), [PR #1001](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1001), [PR #1015](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1015) retain R439; this result leaves B unchanged and changes\none source-access path and helper stock. Their savings are not composed.\nSource inlining and early retirement are prior ideas; the contribution is this\nlegal boundary and its complete paid invoice, not general mechanism priority.\n\nThe all-size/compiler, common-label/mutable-source realization, correlated\nwhole-call hosting, tape/precision and analytic assumptions remain inherited.\nThe cover is compressed, not astronomically enumerated. The inherited invoice\nalso runs historical cited [PR #548](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/548) outer arithmetic; the selected complex cold\nreplay and full selected assembly are not claimed. No practical speedup,\nfull-theorem formal proof, unrestricted optimum or remote CI pass is claimed.\n\nCredit @eumemic, @DreamingOfClouds, Dylan Crow (@utcorvusvolat-dotcom), @DaysSky, @chafreaky, Zhihao Chen (@jacklightChen)\nand the retained E8 supplier lineage. Prepared for Ali Romman (@aliromman),\nwith substantial OpenAI Codex assistance, under Apache-2.0. No independent\nhuman review is implied.\n\nThe coordinator reviewed all new code and the proof, then independently replayed the dirty-column boundary and local controls, the nine-stage native binary, the complete residual-host audit, and the exact supplier invoice. The final invoice matched the saved result.\n",
